# 2026-08-31 F6 skips a spoken reply

## Live, with the real Kokoro engine and a real audio device
A ~20s spoken reply, skip pressed at 2.5s.

  before (one write per sentence):
    pressing F6 at 2.50s
    speak() returned at 4.64s      <- 2.14s of audio after the key

  after (0.1s blocks, flag checked between them):
    pressing F6 at 2.50s
    speak() returned at 2.94s (alive=False)

`stream.write` blocks until the device accepts the data, so a whole sentence
in one call meant the stop flag went unread for the length of that sentence.
The flag was set the entire time; nothing was looking at it.

